title font5x7 tilde-accent vowels corpus -- the fourth lean, GREEN
prompt Read crux/REMEMBER.md and the road-ahead docs; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, one rota deep-read, send often. baton prin recur
think REMEMBER's live edge is the Season G open-media font family; the accented-Latin family reads as two unifying fonts (font5x7_accented lowercase 21, font5x7_upper uppercase 21). Walked the family for the next crux.
think Found a real asymmetry: font5x7_upper draws the uppercase A tilde (U+00C3), yet no lowercase a tilde (U+00E3) or o tilde (U+00F5) is drawn anywhere -- grep found them only as NEGATIVE tests in font5x7_accented (the glyph a corpus proves absent). Portuguese (Sao Paulo, Joao, coracao, irma, nacao) reaches for exactly these nasal vowels. The gap the accented family had carried honestly.
think The accent corpora already prove three leans: acute right (font5x7_latin1), grave left (font5x7_grave), circumflex centered peak (font5x7_circumflex). The tilde is the fourth lean -- a wave spanning both halves. That is the corpus-specific crux to prove beyond the shared round-trip.
think Reused the ASCII-art template from font5x7_grave: same coverage_from_art, build_atlas, ink_count, row_band_ink shape. The tilde mark is the same wave the n tilde carries (rows 0-1: `..#.#`, `.#.#.`), over the grave a/o bodies in rows 2-6.
think Designed three toothed placement guards: top-two-row LEFT-half ink >= 1 and RIGHT-half ink >= 1 (the wave reaches both sides, where acute is right-only and grave left-only), plus row-0 crest right-of-center >= 1 (where a circumflex apex would sit only on center). Each its own bounded reader, no compound assert.
obs GREEN on the first metal run, no red: 2 tilde vowels U+00E3,U+00F5 round-trip byte-identical, present, distinct, legible (ink 16..18 of 35), every mark a wave spanning both halves and cresting right. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, both files plain 7-bit ASCII though the glyphs cover a non-ASCII range (numeric codepoint literals, the ascii-first font-table exception).
obs Docs-sync ratchet, not a sweep: image/README.md accreted the tilde corpus into the accented-Latin family entry, naming the fourth lean and the gap it fills, and added _tilde to the witness-sibling list. Did not claim it into the unifying font5x7_accented (which still tests a tilde absent) -- an honest sibling addition, not a false merge.
obs Rota this lap (d27, item 17) deep-read context/LEXICON.md -- the living vocabulary; nib, waymark, survey, shape, the module names. A corpus named by its plain function (tilde vowels) reads true on its ten-thousandth day, the Comlink tendency and Lindy-first the guide.
